---
// /marks/chinese/imperial-seals: the seals emperors stamped on the paintings
// and calligraphy of the palace collection, Southern Tang to Puyi's court,
// and the sets Qianlong's catalogues stamped together. A catalogue over the
// collection's imperial seal records (family chinese-marks); the records
// already name this page (attributes.intended_page).
import Reference from '../../../layouts/Reference.astro';
import Catalogue from '../../../components/ref/Catalogue.astro';
import AppBox from '../../../components/AppBox.astro';
import { collection } from '../../../lib/portal';
import { imperialSheet, sealSetSheet, SEAL_DYNASTIES, CJK } from '../../../lib/records';
import { articleLd } from '../../../lib/site';

const path = '/marks/chinese/imperial-seals';
const c = collection();
const seals = c.records.filter((r) => r.kind === 'imperial collection seal').map(imperialSheet);
const sets = c.records.filter((r) => r.kind === 'imperial seal set').map(sealSetSheet);
const groups = [
  ...SEAL_DYNASTIES.map(([key, label, blurb]) => ({ key, label, blurb, sheets: seals.filter((s) => s.group === key) })),
  { key: 'sets', label: 'The catalogue sets', blurb: 'A work entered in one of Qianlong’s catalogues was stamped with a fixed set of seals. The set tells which catalogue, and which edition.', sheets: sets },
];
const pictured = seals.filter((s) => s.pics.length).length;
const title = 'Chinese Imperial Collection Seals: Qianlong, Huizong and the Palace Seals | Heirloom';
const description = `${seals.length} seals Chinese emperors stamped on paintings and calligraphy, from the Southern Tang to Puyi’s court, and the seal sets of Qianlong’s catalogues: who each belonged to, where it is found, and the works it is on.`;
const han = [...new Set([...JSON.stringify(groups)].filter((ch) => CJK.test(ch)))].join('') + '乾隆御覽之寶';
---
<Reference {title} {description} {path} jsonld={[articleLd(path, 'Chinese imperial collection seals', description, '2026-11-25')]} {han}>
  <header class="rhead">
    <h1>Imperial collection seals</h1>
    <p class="rhead__lede">Emperors stamped the paintings and calligraphy of the palace with their seals: <span class="han" lang="zh-Hant">乾隆御覽之寶</span>, <span class="tr">“treasure seen by the Qianlong emperor.”</span> Each seal below says whose it was, what kind of seal it is, where on a work it is found, and works it is on.</p>
    <ul class="rhead__meta">
      <li><strong class="num">{seals.length}</strong> seals</li>
      <li><strong class="num">{pictured}</strong> with a picture</li>
      <li><strong class="num">{sets.length}</strong> catalogue sets</li>
    </ul>
  </header>

  <Catalogue {groups} noun={['seal', 'seals and sets']} placeholder="Characters, pinyin or an emperor: 御覽, Qianlong, Huizong" label="Characters, pinyin or an emperor" />

  <section class="ahome__block read" aria-labelledby="rely">
    <h2 id="rely">Before you rely on an imperial seal</h2>
    <p>Imperial seals were copied more than any other: a later painting often carries a full set of Qianlong’s seals to look as if it came from the palace. A seal says whose it claims to be. Whether a work was ever in the palace collection is a question for the catalogues themselves (the <span class="han" lang="zh-Hant">石渠寶笈</span> and <span class="han" lang="zh-Hant">祕殿珠林</span>) and for a specialist who can see the work.</p>
    <p>For the seals of painters and private collectors, see <a href="/marks/chinese/painters/">painters and collectors</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <AppBox text="Photograph the seals. The Advisor reads the characters, names whose seal each claims to be from this same reference, and keeps the reading with the photo." />
</Reference>
